# Umami 3.3.1 (image ghcr.io/umami-software/umami:3.3.1) environment schema
# (@env-spec / varlock format).
#
# The compose previously pinned the floating tag `postgresql-latest`. On
# 2026-09-04 (research date) that tag, `latest`, `3`, `3.3` and `3.3.1` all
# share one digest (sha256:fa32d116cf20cad52cbc3fad9a63b46e7fa02299d8f967168eb453d49c476b4a,
# pushed 2026-08-20, the same day v3.3.1 was released), so the pin below is
# the resolved version, not an upgrade. Umami's mysql-/postgresql- tag
# flavours stopped at 3.0.0: v3 ships ONE image whose prisma/schema.prisma
# declares `provider = "postgresql"` and whose startup script talks to the DB
# through @prisma/adapter-pg, i.e. v3 is Postgres-only and there is no
# `postgresql-3.3.1` tag to pin (404 on ghcr).
#
# Source: grep of `process.env.*` across src/, scripts/, next.config.ts and
# prisma.config.ts at tag v3.3.1, cross-checked against the published
# Environment variables reference and upstream's own docker-compose.yml.
#
# Where they disagree, the code wins:
#
#   * The reference documents none of CLICKHOUSE_URL, KAFKA_URL,
#     KAFKA_BROKER, KAFKA_SASL_MECHANISM, KAFKA_MAX_MESSAGE_BYTES,
#     KAFKA_SSL_ALLOW_UNAUTHORIZED, DATABASE_REPLICA_URL, GEOLITE_DB_PATH,
#     DISABLE_UI, API_URL, LINKS_URL, PIXELS_URL, CLOUD_MODE, CLOUD_URL,
#     TRACKER_SCRIPT_URL, UMAMI_SELF_TRACK or UMAMI_SELF_RECORD. All are read
#     by this version.
#   * The reference files DIRECT_DATABASE_URL, SKIP_DB_CHECK and
#     SKIP_DB_MIGRATION under "build time". In the Docker image they are
#     runtime: `scripts/start-docker.sh` runs `node scripts/check-db.js`
#     (which reads all three) on every container start, before the server.
#   * The reference files GEO_DATABASE_URL under "runtime". It is read only by
#     `scripts/build-geo.js`, which runs during `build-docker`, at build time.
#     The runtime knob for a custom GeoIP database is the undocumented
#     GEOLITE_DB_PATH.
#   * DATABASE_TYPE is vestigial in v3. Nothing under src/ reads it; the only
#     read left is `scripts/check-env.js` (a build script that is not run by
#     the image). The database flavour is derived from the DATABASE_URL scheme
#     in src/lib/db.ts.
#
# BUILD-TIME vs RUNTIME. Umami has no NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables. It gets the
# same effect from next.config.ts, whose `env: { apiUrl, basePath, cloudMode,
# cloudUrl, currentVersion, defaultCurrency, defaultLocale, selfTrack,
# selfRecord }` block inlines those values into the client bundle at
# `next build`, and whose headers()/rewrites()/redirects() are resolved into
# routes-manifest.json at the same time. This image is `output: 'standalone'`,
# so its next.config is already serialized: everything in the "Build-time
# only" section below is baked into the pinned image and setting it on the
# running container does nothing. Two variables are half-and-half and are
# called out where they are declared: COLLECT_API_ENDPOINT and
# TRACKER_SCRIPT_NAME.
#
# The compose prompts for APP_SECRET and POSTGRES_PASSWORD and threads
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD into both DATABASE_URL and the bundled Postgres. Nothing
# else is needed: Umami runs its Prisma migrations on boot and the first visit
# to the UI logs in with the built-in `admin` / `umami` account, which you are
# expected to change immediately.

# @defaultSensitive=false @defaultRequired=infer
# @docs("Umami environment variables", https://docs.umami.is/docs/environment-variables)
# ---

# ─── Core ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Connection string, assembled by the compose from the prompted
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD and the database service's hostname. The only variable
# Umami genuinely cannot start without: scripts/check-db.js throws on a
# missing value, and src/lib/db.ts derives the database flavour from this
# URL's scheme (`postgres:` and `postgresql:` both mean Postgres; v3 supports
# nothing else). A `?schema=` query parameter is honoured. Point it elsewhere
# only if you are moving to an external Postgres, at which point the bundled
# one is unused.
# @required
# @sensitive
# @docs("Umami installation", https://docs.umami.is/docs/install)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://umami:${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}@${{stack.db.HOST}}:5432/umami

# Set by the compose to `postgresql`. Vestigial at this version: no code under
# src/ reads it, and the only remaining read is in scripts/check-env.js, a
# build-time script the image never runs. Kept because the compose sets it and
# because upstream's docs still list it as required for custom Docker builds.
DATABASE_TYPE=postgresql

# THE signing key for the whole instance. src/lib/crypto.ts `secret()` hashes
# it, and src/lib/auth.ts signs and verifies every auth JWT and every share
# token with the result. Two consequences worth understanding:
#
#   1. If it is unset, `secret()` falls back to hashing DATABASE_URL. Anyone
#      who knows the database connection string (a teammate with DB access, a
#      leaked backup, a compose file in a screenshot) can then mint a valid
#      session token for any user without ever touching the login form. Always
#      set it; the compose prompts for it.
#   2. Changing it invalidates every existing session and share link at once,
#      and because src/lib/crypto.ts `uuid()` mixes `secret()` into its v5
#      derivation, it also changes the derived visitor session IDs, so
#      returning visitors are counted as new after the swap.
#
# Generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`. Unique per installation.
# @required
# @sensitive
APP_SECRET=

# Direct (unpooled) Postgres connection string used ONLY by
# `prisma migrate deploy` inside scripts/check-db.js, which the container runs
# on every start. Set it when DATABASE_URL points at a transaction pooler
# (PgBouncer, Supavisor, Neon pooled endpoint) that cannot run migrations.
# Defaults to DATABASE_URL. Irrelevant with the bundled Postgres.
# @sensitive
DIRECT_DATABASE_URL=

# Read-replica connection string. When set, src/lib/prisma.ts routes read
# queries to it and keeps writes on DATABASE_URL. Undocumented upstream. An
# out-of-date or unreachable replica shows stale or empty reports while
# collection keeps working, which is a confusing failure mode. Leave empty
# unless you actually run one.
# @sensitive
DATABASE_REPLICA_URL=

# Skips the whole check-db.js step at container start: no connectivity probe,
# no Postgres-version check (minimum 9.4), and no migrations. Only useful if
# you migrate out of band; leaving it set across an upgrade means the schema
# is never brought forward and the app fails on the first query.
# @type=boolean
SKIP_DB_CHECK=

# Runs the connectivity and version checks but skips `prisma migrate deploy`.
# Same upgrade caveat as SKIP_DB_CHECK.
# @type=boolean
SKIP_DB_MIGRATION=

# Address and port the Next.js standalone server binds. Both are already baked
# into the image (`ENV HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0`, `ENV PORT=3000`) and the compose
# exposes container port 3000 with no override, so PORT here is that port's
# twin: change it without changing the exposed port and routing breaks.
# Binding HOSTNAME to 127.0.0.1 makes the container unreachable from the
# stack network.
HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0
# @type=port
PORT=3000

# ─── Authentication and access ─────────────────────────────────────────────

# 64-character hex string (a 256-bit key) that AES-256-GCM-encrypts every
# stored TOTP secret and backup code (src/lib/two-factor/crypto.ts, which
# validates the value against /^[0-9a-fA-F]{64}$/). Without it (or with a
# malformed value), no user can enable two-factor authentication: v3.3.1
# hardened the 2FA APIs to refuse the setup, verify, disable and admin-reset
# routes with a `two-factor-error-not-configured` response instead of failing
# obscurely. Losing or rotating it makes existing 2FA enrolments
# undecryptable, locking those users out until an admin resets their 2FA.
# Generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`. New in 3.3.0.
# @sensitive
# @type=string(matches=/^[0-9a-fA-F]{64}$/)
# @docs("Two-factor authentication", https://docs.umami.is/docs/two-factor-authentication)
TWO_FACTOR_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# AUTH BYPASS: set this and /login, /login/two-factor and /logout all render
# nothing (src/app/login/page.tsx, src/app/login/two-factor/page.tsx,
# src/app/logout/page.tsx). It is meant for deployments that put their own
# SSO/reverse-proxy authentication in front of Umami. It does NOT add
# authentication of its own, so if the instance is reachable without that
# proxy the dashboard and its API are simply open. Leave empty unless an
# external authenticator is definitely in the request path.
# @type=boolean
DISABLE_LOGIN=

# Renders an empty <body> for the whole app shell (src/app/layout.tsx),
# leaving only the collection and API endpoints. For collector-only
# deployments. Undocumented upstream. Not a security control: the API is
# untouched.
# @type=boolean
DISABLE_UI=

# Disables every outbound network call the server makes (telemetry, the
# update check, and the favicon service that renders website icons). The
# honest choice for an air-gapped or privacy-strict install; the UI simply
# loses its site icons.
# @type=boolean
PRIVATE_MODE=

# Exposes the internal test console at {host}/console, where an admin can
# hand-fire pageviews and events at a website. Handy while wiring up
# tracking, noise in your own data if you forget it is on.
# @type=boolean
ENABLE_TEST_CONSOLE=

# Umami Cloud mode. Only meaningful for umami.is' own hosted service: it
# hides login/logout, rewrites /script.js to cloud.umami.is and short-circuits
# the record API. It is also inlined into the client bundle at build time, so
# setting it on this self-hosted image only produces the server half of that
# behaviour. Leave empty.
# @type=boolean
CLOUD_MODE=

# ─── Data collection ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# By default /api/send and /api/record drop requests whose user agent matches
# the `isbot` list. Setting this counts bots as visitors, usually a mistake,
# occasionally what you want when a legitimate client is misidentified.
# @type=boolean
DISABLE_BOT_CHECK=

# Comma-delimited list of IP addresses and CIDR ranges dropped at collection
# time (src/lib/detect.ts `hasBlockedIp`). The usual use is excluding your
# office or home address from your own statistics. e.g.
# `192.168.0.1, 10.0.0.0/24, 2001:db8::/32`.
# @docs("Exclude my own visits", https://docs.umami.is/docs/exclude-my-own-visits)
IGNORE_IP=

# HTTP header to read the client IP from, when the reverse proxy in front of
# Umami uses a non-standard one. Empty means the built-in list
# (x-forwarded-for, forwarded, cf-connecting-ip, …) is tried in order. Getting
# this wrong makes every visitor share the proxy's IP, which collapses
# sessions and geolocation into one.
# @docs("Enable Cloudflare headers", https://docs.umami.is/docs/enable-cloudflare-headers)
CLIENT_IP_HEADER=

# Ignores the CDN geolocation headers (Cloudflare, Vercel, …) and always uses
# the bundled MaxMind database. Set it when the proxy sends only a country
# header, which otherwise suppresses region and city entirely.
# @type=boolean
SKIP_LOCATION_HEADERS=

# Strips the trailing slash from incoming tracked URLs so `/about/` and
# `/about` are one page. v3.3.1 fixed this to leave the root path `/` alone
# rather than reducing it to an empty string.
# @type=boolean
REMOVE_TRAILING_SLASH=

# How often the salt behind anonymous session identifiers rotates
# (src/lib/crypto.ts `getSalt`). Shorter rotation is more private and breaks
# returning-visitor continuity sooner; the value is read per request, so
# changing it re-buckets sessions from that point on. Anything other than
# `day` or `week` falls through to `month`. New in 3.1.0.
# @type=enum(day, week, month)
SALT_ROTATION=month

# Generates UUIDv7 instead of UUIDv4 for new random identifiers. v7 IDs are
# time-ordered, which indexes better in Postgres, but they encode their
# creation timestamp. Deterministic IDs derived from analytics data are
# unaffected. New in 3.0.2.
# @type=boolean
USE_UUIDV7=

# Serves the collection endpoint at a custom path instead of /api/send, to get
# past ad blockers. HALF RUNTIME: scripts/update-tracker.js runs at container
# start and does rewrite public/script.js to post here, but the Next.js
# rewrite that maps this path back to /api/send is baked into
# routes-manifest.json at image build. On this prebuilt image the tracker will
# therefore POST to a 404. Needs a custom build to actually work.
# @docs("Bypass ad blockers", https://docs.umami.is/docs/bypass-ad-blockers)
COLLECT_API_ENDPOINT=

# Alternative filename(s) for the tracker script, comma-separated, again to
# get past ad blockers. HALF RUNTIME for the same reason: /api/config reports
# the name so the UI shows the right snippet, but the rewrite from that name
# to /script.js is baked at build time, so the snippet the UI hands you 404s
# on this image unless it was built with the same value.
TRACKER_SCRIPT_NAME=

# ─── Privacy, telemetry and UI ─────────────────────────────────────────────

# Umami posts anonymous usage telemetry on build and exposes /telemetry.js.
# Set this to opt out. PRIVATE_MODE also covers it.
# @type=boolean
DISABLE_TELEMETRY=

# Stops the dashboard checking github for newer Umami releases and showing the
# update banner. Useful when the image tag is managed for you, as it is here.
# @type=boolean
DISABLE_UPDATES=

# Template for the service that renders website icons in the dashboard, with
# `{{domain}}` substituted. Empty uses
# https://icons.duckduckgo.com/ip3/{{domain}}.ico. Any value here sends the
# domains you track to a third party, which is why PRIVATE_MODE disables it
# outright.
FAVICON_URL=

# Absolute path inside the container to a MaxMind-format GeoLite2-City.mmdb.
# Empty uses the copy baked into the image at /app/geo/GeoLite2-City.mmdb,
# which ages with the tag. Mount a fresher database here if location accuracy
# matters. Undocumented upstream.
# @docs("GeoLite2 free geolocation data", https://dev.maxmind.com/geoip/geolite2-free-geolocation-data)
GEOLITE_DB_PATH=

# ─── Optional external services ────────────────────────────────────────────

# Redis connection string. Not part of this stack, so leave empty and Umami's
# Redis-backed caching stays off (src/lib/redis.ts gates on this variable
# alone). Point it at a Redis you run when a single instance stops keeping up
# or you run more than one replica. New in 3.0.1.
# @sensitive
# @type=url
# @docs("Enable Redis", https://docs.umami.is/docs/enable-redis)
REDIS_URL=

# ClickHouse connection string. Setting it switches every analytics read and
# write from Postgres to ClickHouse, which is how umami.is runs at scale and
# is a one-way move for your data: the Postgres tables are then no longer the
# source of truth, and relational-only features (session deletion, some
# property reports) turn themselves off. Undocumented upstream. Requires
# CLOUD_URL and REDIS_URL alongside it.
# @sensitive
CLICKHOUSE_URL=

# Kafka ingestion, used together with ClickHouse: collection events are
# produced to Kafka instead of written directly. Both KAFKA_URL (whose
# userinfo carries the SASL credentials) and KAFKA_BROKER (comma-separated
# broker list) must be set or src/lib/kafka.ts stays disabled. Undocumented
# upstream.
# @sensitive
KAFKA_URL=
KAFKA_BROKER=
# SASL mechanism for the above. Defaults to `plain` when empty.
# @type=enum(plain, scram-sha-256, scram-sha-512)
KAFKA_SASL_MECHANISM=
# Producer message-size ceiling in bytes. Empty uses kafkajs' own default.
# @type=number
KAFKA_MAX_MESSAGE_BYTES=
# Accepts a Kafka broker's TLS certificate without verifying it. Only the
# exact string `true` disables verification. Turning off certificate checks on
# a link carrying raw analytics traffic is a real downgrade. Prefer fixing
# the CA bundle.
# @type=boolean
KAFKA_SSL_ALLOW_UNAUTHORIZED=

# Base URLs advertised by /api/config for Umami's hosted Links and Pixels
# products. Self-hosted instances have no such services, so leaving these
# empty is what hides those sections. Undocumented upstream.
# @type=url
LINKS_URL=
# @type=url
PIXELS_URL=

# ─── Diagnostics ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Logs every database query to the container log (src/lib/prisma.ts,
# src/lib/clickhouse.ts). Verbose and it prints query parameters, so treat the
# logs as sensitive while it is on. Debugging only.
# @type=boolean
LOG_QUERY=

# Namespace filter for the `debug` package, which every Umami module logs
# through. Useful values: `umami:auth`, `umami:prisma`, `umami:clickhouse`,
# `umami:kafka`, `umami:middleware`, or `umami:*` for all of it.
DEBUG=

# Baked into the image as `production`; setting it from the compose has no
# effect on the prebuilt bundle. Listed because the code branches on it.
# @type=enum(production, development)
NODE_ENV=production

# ─── Build-time only (no effect on this image) ─────────────────────────────
# Everything below is read by next.config.ts or by a build script. This image
# is a `next build --turbo` standalone output, so the resolved config
# (headers, rewrites, redirects and the inlined client `env` block) is already
# serialized inside it. These are declared for completeness and so the editor
# does not present them as a fix when they do not work; changing any of them
# requires building a custom image.

# Subdirectory to host Umami under, e.g. `/analytics`. A Dockerfile ARG
# (`ARG BASE_PATH`), so it is fixed at build. Not present in the pinned
# image's runtime env at all.
BASE_PATH=

# Space-delimited list of URLs allowed to embed Umami in an iframe; feeds the
# `frame-ancestors` directive of the Content-Security-Policy header
# (src/lib/csp.ts, called from next.config.ts). Empty means `'self'` only.
ALLOWED_FRAME_URLS=

# Adds a Strict-Transport-Security header (2 years, includeSubDomains,
# preload) to every response. Baked into the header set at build.
# @type=boolean
FORCE_SSL=

# Seconds a CORS preflight for /api/* is cached. Empty means 86400.
# @type=number
CORS_MAX_AGE=

# Serves the API under an extra path prefix and adds that origin to the CSP.
# Both halves are build-time. Undocumented upstream.
API_URL=

# Locale and currency the UI falls back to before a user picks their own,
# e.g. `en-US` and `USD`. Inlined into the client bundle. New in 3.1.0.
DEFAULT_LOCALE=
DEFAULT_CURRENCY=

# Rewrites /script.js to an externally hosted tracker. Undocumented upstream.
TRACKER_SCRIPT_URL=

# Website IDs Umami uses to track and session-record its own dashboard.
# Inlined into the client bundle as `selfTrack` / `selfRecord`. Undocumented
# upstream.
UMAMI_SELF_TRACK=
UMAMI_SELF_RECORD=

# Base URL of the Umami Cloud API. Only for the hosted service; when set,
# scripts/check-env.js also demands CLICKHOUSE_URL and REDIS_URL.
# Undocumented upstream.
CLOUD_URL=

# Where scripts/build-geo.js downloads the GeoIP database from during the
# image build. Empty falls back to a MaxMind download URL built from
# MAXMIND_LICENSE_KEY, or to the node-geolite2-redist copy when that is empty
# too. The runtime equivalent is GEOLITE_DB_PATH, above.
# @type=url
GEO_DATABASE_URL=
# @sensitive
MAXMIND_LICENSE_KEY=

# Skip, or force, the GeoIP download step of the build. SKIP_BUILD_GEO wins.
# @type=boolean
SKIP_BUILD_GEO=
# @type=boolean
BUILD_GEO=

# ─── Bundled Postgres ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The stack runs its own postgres:16-alpine. Umami applies its Prisma
# migrations against it on every container start; there is no separate
# migration step. check-db.js refuses anything older than PostgreSQL 9.4.

# Role Umami connects as, created by the Postgres image on first boot. It is
# baked into DATABASE_URL above; changing it here alone only breaks the pair.
POSTGRES_USER=umami

# Password for that role, used by both the database container and
# DATABASE_URL. It is only reachable on the stack's private network, but note
# that it is also the fallback signing key: with APP_SECRET unset, anyone who
# can reconstruct DATABASE_URL from this can forge Umami sessions.
# @required
# @sensitive
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# Database created on first boot. Baked into DATABASE_URL above.
POSTGRES_DB=umami
